{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q4", "request_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z-0009", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:10.282+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 29.007, "patience_s": 14.2, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 814.9, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z-0009", "question": "Per Table 1, how does self-attention compare with recurrent layers on complexity per layer, sequential operations and maximum path length?", "kind": "answer", "level": 1, "text": "Self‑attention layers have a per‑layer computational complexity of \\(O(n^{2}\\,d)\\), require only a constant number of sequential operations \\(O(1)\\), and have a maximum path length of \\(O(1)\\) between any two positions [S2].  \nRecurrent layers, in contrast, cost \\(O(n\\,d^{2})\\) per layer, need \\(O(n)\\) sequential operations, and their maximum path length also scales as \\(O(n)\\) [S2].  \nThus, self‑attention is computationally more expensive than recurrent layers only when the sequence length \\(n\\) exceeds the representation dimension \\(d\\), but it offers far greater parallelism (constant‑time sequential depth) and a dramatically shorter longest dependency path [S1][S2].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.6-7 §4", "pid": "attention:2400:0012", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b011", "attention-p06-b012", "attention-p06-b013", "attention-p06-b014", "attention-p07-b001"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.5-6 §3.4", "pid": "attention:2400:0010", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p05-b017", "attention-p05-b018", "attention-p06-b001", "attention-p06-b002"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.7 §4", "pid": "attention:2400:0013", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p07-b002", "attention-p07-b003"]}], "notice": "answered by a fallback model because the preferred one was busy; checked for citations only (no second-model check)", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 249, "completion_tokens": 62}, {"step": "draft", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1181, "completion_tokens": 188}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 1.0, "model": null, "outcome": "full (other model)", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 2.551656000003277, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 2.7039882999961264, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 1.0, "end_ms": 267.3, "model": null, "outcome": "router", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:understand", "start_ms": 1.0, "end_ms": 1.1, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:understand", "start_ms": 1.1, "end_ms": 267.2, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 267.3, "end_ms": 267.6, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "Table 1 self-attention recurrent cost per layer sequential operations longest dependency path Per Table 1, how does self-attention compare with recurrent layers on complexity per layer, sequential operations and maximum path length?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "evidence": {"best": 1.0, "union": 1.0, "top_bm25": 82.609, "query_terms": 13}}}, {"name": "decide", "start_ms": 267.6, "end_ms": 267.7, "model": null, "outcome": "draft", "detail": {"best": 1.0, "union": 1.0, "top_bm25": 82.609, "query_terms": 13}}, {"name": "draft", "start_ms": 267.7, "end_ms": 813.8, "model": null, "outcome": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "detail": {"level": "full (other model)"}}, {"name": "wait:draft", "start_ms": 267.7, "end_ms": 267.8, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_