{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q13", "request_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z-0010", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:12.082+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 30.783, "patience_s": 44.99, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 668.1, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z-0010", "question": "In H-Net, what do the encoder and decoder networks do, and at what resolution do they run?", "kind": "answer", "level": 2, "text": "A natural question arises: does the importance of Mamba layers (i) stem specifically from processing fine-grained byte inputs, or (ii) because they are better for compressing information into the next stage, even at coarser input resolutions? [S1]", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2507.07955v2 pp.19-20 §3.3", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0035", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p19-b005", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b006", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b007", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b009", "dynamic_chunking-p20-b001"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.2 §1", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0003", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p02-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p02-b009", "dynamic_chunking-p02-b010"]}], "notice": "shorter answer from fewer passages, without the extra checks, because the service is busy", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 239, "completion_tokens": 50}, {"step": "draft", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1245, "completion_tokens": 69}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.7, "model": null, "outcome": "full (other model)", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-12