{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q8", "request_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z-0018", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:55.045+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 73.751, "patience_s": 17.49, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 1242.1, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload-20261110T183141Z-0018", "question": "What are Moshi's main components and what does each do?", "kind": "answer", "level": 1, "text": "Moshi’s architecture is built around three core components: the Helium text‑language‑model backbone, the Mimi neural audio codec, and the streaming Depth Transformer that jointly processes two audio streams and time‑aligned text tokens [S2]. Helium supplies strong reasoning and linguistic knowledge to the system by providing pre‑trained text tokens that are used as prefixes for semantic generation, thereby improving factuality and linguistic quality during dialogue [S1][S2]. Mimi encodes raw audio into discrete acoustic tokens using residual vector quantization and distills semantic information into the first token level, enabling the model to synthesize intelligible, high‑quality speech directly from its predictions without a separate TTS stage [S1][S3]. The Depth Transformer, designed for streaming inference, hierarchically generates semantic and acoustic tokens for both the user and Moshi while aligning text tokens via the Inner Monologue procedure, allowing full‑duplex, real‑time spoken dialogue without explicit speaker‑turn modeling [S1][S3].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2410.00037v1 pp.6-7 §3.1", "pid": "moshi:2400:0009", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p06-b005", "moshi-p07-b001", "moshi-p07-b002"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.6 §2", "pid": "moshi:2400:0008", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p06-b001", "moshi-p06-b002"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.3 §1", "pid": "moshi:2400:0003", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p03-b003", "moshi-p03-b004", "moshi-p03-b005", "moshi-p03-b006", "moshi-p03-b007", "moshi-p03-b008"]}], "notice": "answered by a fallback model because the preferred one was busy; checked for citations only (no second-model check)", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 231, "completion_tokens": 82}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1763, "completion_tokens": 383}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.8, "model": null, "outcome": "full (other model)", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 10.381354500008456, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 0.0, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-20b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 374.2, "model": null, "outcome": "router", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 0.9, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:understand", "start_ms": 0.9, "end_ms": 374.2, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 374.2, "end_ms": 374.8, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "Moshi architecture Inner Monologue Time Extended Transformer TTT Residual Vector Quantization RVQ streaming autoregressive What are Moshi's main components and what does each do?", "papers": ["moshi"], "k": 3, "evidence": {"best": 1.0, "union": 1.0, "top_bm25": 28.523, "query_terms": 5}}}, {"name": "decide", "start_ms": 374.8, "end_ms": 374.9, "model": null, "outcome": "draft", "detail": {"best": 1.0, "union": 1.0, "top_bm25": 28.523, "query_terms": 5}}, {"name": "draft", "start_ms": 374.9, "end_ms": 1240.6, "model": null, "outcome": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "detail": {"level": "full 